--TEST--
A class constant whose value folds to nothing is refused where it is read and not where it is declared — `rule:classes/no-free-functions-or-constants`, `rule:attributes/payload-is-a-compile-time-constant`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `rule:classes/no-free-functions-or-constants` inlines a class constant at every use site, so a declaration the
// constant folder cannot reduce to a value leaves a read with nothing to
// lower. The three shapes `rule:attributes/payload-is-a-compile-time-constant` admits as constants elsewhere — another
// class's `const`, an enum case and `Foo::class` — have no constant form here
// yet, written on their own or nested inside an array.
final class Base {
    public const int ONE = 1;
}

final class Cfg {
    public const string NAME = Cfg::class;
    public const array<int> DERIVED = [Base::ONE];
    // Declared and never read, which is legal: a constant nobody names costs
    // nothing and has no wrong behaviour to report, so the refusal is on the
    // read alone and this line contributes no diagnostic.
    public const array<int> UNUSED = [Base::ONE];
}

echo Cfg::NAME, "\n";
echo Cfg::DERIVED[0], "\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0792]: `Cfg::NAME` has no compile-time value to inline
   --> case.nvs:20:6
%A
error[E0792]: `Cfg::DERIVED` has no compile-time value to inline
   --> case.nvs:21:6
%A
error: aborting due to 2 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
